title: Fail at start-up on an unusable wiki_root (and optionally when --git cannot
  be honoured)
updated: 2026-11-03T19:27:41Z
---

Found by p5-mcp-hub's k29 research. A missing wiki_root starts normally and every call answers 'Invalid wiki_root: .', so a host like mcp-hub shows the upstream as healthy instead of failed. Refuse to start with a clear message. Consider an opt-in that also refuses to start when --git is requested but Git::Raw or the repository is missing, so a shared store never silently runs without history.

From p5-mcp-hub (k37 design, 2026-11-03): mcp-hub expands nothing in a class entry's args and starts mcp-wiki unattended, so a bad wiki_root shows up there as a 'healthy' upstream whose every call fails. Hub users hit this directly — worth a higher priority.
